From 72087e15c76df1b7cd1293029f298f2108b0298f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kazhiramatsu <kazutakehiramatsu@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 00:25:55 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] draft(A6-41 item 2): super paths of decorated static
 initializers and static blocks

standard_decorators.rs (transformESDecorators @6.0.3, _tsc.js:100154-100480):
- class and class-element frames carry classSuper; updateState derives the
  (classThis, classSuper) receiver pair.
- visitor / discardedValueVisitor value use (for-statement initializer and
  incrementor, expression statements, comma lists, parentheses, partially
  emitted expressions).
- super property/element reads -> Reflect.get(_classSuper, key, _classThis)
  (original/range = the super token), calls -> .call(_classThis, ...),
  tagged templates -> .bind(_classThis), assignments (plain, compound and
  logical through a stabilized key temp, hoisted result temp when the value
  is used), prefix/postfix updates through
  expandPreOrPostfixIncrementOrDecrementExpression, destructuring assignment
  targets (array/object patterns, defaults, rest) through
  ({ set value(_a) { Reflect.set(...) } }).value.
- temporaries hoist into the innermost lexical environment (static block
  var, property-initializer IIFE).

Witness group decorator-super-paths: 7/42 -> 34/42 exact twice
(target/dec-next-runs/item2-r1); all ES2022/ESNext commands exact. ES2015
residuals: the two adjacent controls fail identically at baseline (class-
fields ES2015 Reflect lowering maps), one map-only destructuring command, and
a spurious outer super alias allocated by the ES2015 class-fields lowering
when only a nested class references super.
